module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.ClosedImmersionFinitePresentationLimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FinitePresentation.LocallyNoetherian
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Functorial
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Finiteness
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Properties, Tag 01PG at a sheaf of ideals, and Limits, Tag 09ZP

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsSupOfFinitePresentation` asks that a quasi-coherent
sheaf of ideals be the supremum of the sheaves of ideals below it which are finitely generated
on every affine open. It is the hypothesis under which
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLimit_finitePresentationCone` exhibits a closed subscheme as the limit of
its finite-presentation enlargements. This file proves it for a quasi-compact and
quasi-separated scheme, which is Properties, Tag 01PG read in the lattice
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`, and so obtains Limits, Tag 09ZP.

Four things go into it.

The commutative algebra behind the extension step: an ideal has a finitely generated subideal
with the same image under any finite family of ring maps along which that image is finitely
generated. Nothing about schemes enters.

The local nature of finite generation for a sheaf of ideals: it is enough to check it on a
basic-open cover of an affine open, and hence on any family of affine opens covering the
scheme. The ring-theoretic core is `Ideal.fg_of_localizationSpan` and the geometric input is
that the ideal at a basic open is the image of the ideal above it,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal_basicOpen`.

A local form of the kernel of a quasi-compact morphism: a section over an affine open lies in
the kernel sheaf of ideals as soon as it does over a family of affine opens covering the
*preimage* of that open. This is what makes the two-chart gluing of Tag 01PF available at a
sheaf of ideals: the glued object is an intersection with a pushforward along the inclusion of
a chart, and the inequality needed over the old charts is not the one the Galois connection
between pushforward and pullback supplies — that one is global, and globally false here.

Finally the locally Noetherian case, which needs none of the above: over a locally Noetherian
scheme *every* closed immersion is of finite presentation, so the indexing family contains the
sheaf of ideals itself and the supremum is attained.

## Main results

* `Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_fg_le_forall_map_eq`: the algebraic extension step.
* `Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.fg_ideal_of_fg_cover`: finite generation of a sheaf of ideals is
  local on the scheme.
* `Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_le_fg_at_chart` and
  `Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_le_fg_of_list`: the two-chart step and the induction of
  Properties, Tag 01PF read at a sheaf of ideals.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_qcqs`: **Properties, Tag 01PG at a sheaf of
  ideals**, and `AlgebraicGeometry.isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_isLocallyNoetherian` for a
  locally Noetherian scheme.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isLimit_finitePresentationCone_of_qcqs`: **Limits, Tag 09ZP**.

## Implementation notes

The only value of the pushforward that has to be computed is the one over the chart itself
(`Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.ideal_map_ofIdealTop_ι`); its values over the basic opens of the
chart then come from the sheaf-of-ideals axiom
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal_basicOpen`, which is why the covering family
of the two-chart step is taken to consist of basic opens of the chart rather than of arbitrary
affine opens inside it.

The finitely generated subideal is produced without choosing preimages of generators: the
image of an ideal is the supremum, over the elements of the ideal, of the principal ideals
generated by their images, and an element of a supremum of submodules lies in a finite
subsupremum (`Submodule.mem_iSup_iff_exists_finset`). Collecting those finite index sets over
the finitely many generators of the image gives the subideal directly.

`@[stacks 09ZP]` is **withheld** from
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLimit_finitePresentationCone_of_isLocallyNoetherian`: the tag assumes the
target quasi-compact and quasi-separated, and `IsLocallyNoetherian` is neither implied by that
nor implies it. No tag is placed on the finite-generation results either; the locality of
finite generation is not the content of a single tag of the source.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09ZP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09ZP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01TX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01TX)
-/
@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry Stacks.Flatness

universe u v

namespace Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType

/-- An ideal has a finitely generated subideal with the same image under a given ring map, as
soon as that image is finitely generated: finitely many elements of the ideal already carry
the finitely many generators of the image. -/
theorem exists_fg_le_map_eq {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S)
    (a : Ideal R) (h : (a.map φ).FG) :
    ∃ b : Ideal R, b ≤ a ∧ b.FG ∧ b.map φ = a.map φ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := h
  have hmap : a.map φ = ⨆ x : a, Ideal.span {φ (x : R)} := by
    refine le_antisymm ?_ (iSup_le fun x ↦
      (Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem _).2 (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem φ x.2))
    rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro r hr
    exact Ideal.mem_comap.2 (Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem (⟨r, hr⟩ : a) (Ideal.subset_span rfl))
  have hfin : ∀ y ∈ t, ∃ s : Finset a, y ∈ ⨆ x ∈ s, Ideal.span {φ (x : R)} := fun y hy ↦
    Submodule.mem_iSup_iff_exists_finset.1 (hmap ▸ ht ▸ Ideal.subset_span hy)
  choose s hs using hfin
  set S₀ : Finset a := t.attach.biUnion (fun y ↦ s y.1 y.2) with hS₀
  have hle : Ideal.span ((S₀.image (fun x : a ↦ (x : R)) : Finset R) : Set R) ≤ a := by
    rw [Ideal.span_le]
    intro r hr
    simp only [Finset.coe_image, Set.mem_image, Finset.mem_coe] at hr
    obtain ⟨x, -, rfl⟩ := hr
    exact x.2
  refine ⟨_, hle, Submodule.fg_span (Set.toFinite _), le_antisymm (Ideal.map_mono hle) ?_⟩
  rw [← ht, Ideal.span_le]
  intro y hy
  refine (iSup₂_le fun x hx ↦ (Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem _).2 ?_) (hs y hy)
  refine Ideal.mem_map_of_mem φ (Ideal.subset_span ?_)
  simp only [Finset.coe_image, Set.mem_image, Finset.mem_coe]
  exact ⟨x, Finset.mem_biUnion.2 ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, Finset.mem_attach _ _, hx⟩, rfl⟩

/-- An ideal has a single finitely generated subideal with the same image under each of a
finite family of ring maps, as soon as all those images are finitely generated. This is the
commutative algebra of the extension step of Properties, Tag 01PF read at a sheaf of ideals:
the family of ring maps is the family of restrictions to the affine opens of an intersection
of two charts. -/
theorem exists_fg_le_forall_map_eq {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {ι : Type*} [Finite ι]
    {S : ι → Type v} [∀ i, CommRing (S i)] (φ : ∀ i, R →+* S i) (a : Ideal R)
    (h : ∀ i, (a.map (φ i)).FG) :
    ∃ b : Ideal R, b ≤ a ∧ b.FG ∧ ∀ i, b.map (φ i) = a.map (φ i) := by
  choose b hble hbfg hbeq using fun i ↦ exists_fg_le_map_eq (φ i) a (h i)
  refine ⟨⨆ i, b i, iSup_le hble, Submodule.fg_iSup _ hbfg, fun i ↦
    le_antisymm (Ideal.map_mono (iSup_le hble)) ?_⟩
  rw [← hbeq i]
  exact Ideal.map_mono (le_iSup b i)

variable {Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Finite generation of a sheaf of ideals over an affine open may be checked on a cover of
that open by basic opens: the ideal over a basic open is the localization of the ideal above
it, so `Ideal.fg_of_localizationSpan` applies. -/
theorem fg_ideal_of_fg_basicOpen (I : Y.IdealSheafData) (A : Y.affineOpens)
    (s : Set Γ(Y, A.1)) (hs : Ideal.span s = ⊤)
    (h : ∀ g : s, (I.ideal (Y.affineBasicOpen (U := A) g.1)).FG) :
    (I.ideal A).FG := by
  refine Ideal.fg_of_localizationSpan s hs fun g ↦ ?_
  have hL := A.2.isLocalization_basicOpen (g : Γ(Y, A.1))
  have hfg := h g
  rw [← I.map_ideal_basicOpen A (g : Γ(Y, A.1))] at hfg
  have hres : (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le (g : Γ(Y, A.1)))).op).hom =
      algebraMap Γ(Y, A.1) Γ(Y, Y.basicOpen (g : Γ(Y, A.1))) := rfl
  rw [hres] at hfg
  let e : Γ(Y, Y.basicOpen (g : Γ(Y, A.1))) ≃ₐ[Γ(Y, A.1)]
      Localization.Away (g : Γ(Y, A.1)) :=
    IsLocalization.algEquiv (Submonoid.powers (g : Γ(Y, A.1))) _ _
  rw [← AlgHom.comp_algebraMap e.toAlgHom, ← Ideal.map_map]
  exact hfg.map _

/-- A sheaf of ideals finitely generated over an affine open is so over every smaller one. -/
private theorem fg_ideal_of_le {I : Y.IdealSheafData} {U V : Y.affineOpens} (h : U ≤ V)
    (hV : (I.ideal V).FG) : (I.ideal U).FG := by
  rw [← I.map_ideal h]
  exact hV.map _

/-- A sheaf of ideals finitely generated over each member of a family of affine opens covering
the scheme is finitely generated over *every* affine open. -/
theorem fg_ideal_of_fg_cover (I : Y.IdealSheafData) {ι : Type*} (V : ι → Y.affineOpens)
    (hV : ⨆ i, (V i).1 = ⊤) (h : ∀ i, (I.ideal (V i)).FG) (A : Y.affineOpens) :
    (I.ideal A).FG := by
  have hex : ∀ x : A.1, ∃ (i : ι) (r : Γ(Y, A.1)) (rV : Γ(Y, (V i).1)),
      Y.basicOpen r = Y.basicOpen rV ∧ x.1 ∈ Y.basicOpen r := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp (hV.ge (Set.mem_univ x.1))
    exact ⟨i, exists_basicOpen_le_affine_inter A.2 (V i).2 _ ⟨x.2, hi⟩⟩
  choose i r rV e hxr using hex
  have hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range r) = ⊤ := by
    rw [← A.2.self_le_iSup_basicOpen_iff]
    exact fun x hxA ↦ TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨_, _, rfl⟩, hxr ⟨x, hxA⟩⟩
  refine fg_ideal_of_fg_basicOpen I A (Set.range r) hspan ?_
  rintro ⟨-, x, rfl⟩
  have heq : Y.affineBasicOpen (U := A) (r x) = Y.affineBasicOpen (U := V (i x)) (rV x) :=
    Subtype.ext (e x)
  exact heq ▸ fg_ideal_of_le (Y.affineBasicOpen_le _) (h (i x))

/-- A section over an affine open lies in the kernel sheaf of ideals of a quasi-compact
morphism as soon as its restrictions to a family of affine opens covering the *preimage* of
that open do. The family is required to cover the preimage, not the open itself, which is what
makes this usable for a morphism whose image misses part of the open; the proof is the
separatedness half of the sheaf condition on the source. -/
theorem mem_ker_ideal_of_forall_restrict {T : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ Y) [QuasiCompact g]
    (A : Y.affineOpens) {ι : Type*} (D : ι → Y.affineOpens) (hDA : ∀ t, (D t).1 ≤ A.1)
    (hcov : g ⁻¹ᵁ A.1 ≤ ⨆ t, g ⁻¹ᵁ (D t).1) {y : Γ(Y, A.1)}
    (hy : ∀ t, (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hDA t)).op).hom y ∈ g.ker.ideal (D t)) :
    y ∈ g.ker.ideal A := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.ker_apply, RingHom.mem_ker]
  apply T.IsSheaf.section_ext
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨t, hxt⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp (hcov hx)
  have hsub : g ⁻¹ᵁ (D t).1 ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ A.1 :=
    leOfHom ((TopologicalSpace.Opens.map g.base).map (homOfLE (hDA t)))
  refine ⟨g ⁻¹ᵁ (D t).1, hsub, hxt, ?_⟩
  have hnat := g.naturality (U := (D t).1) (U' := A.1) (homOfLE (hDA t)).op
  have heq : (T.presheaf.map ((TopologicalSpace.Opens.map g.base).map (homOfLE (hDA t))).op).hom
      ((g.app A.1).hom y) = (g.app (D t).1).hom
        ((Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hDA t)).op).hom y) := by
    have h2 := congrArg (fun φ ↦ CommRingCat.Hom.hom φ y) hnat.symm
    simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply] at h2
    exact h2
  have h3 := hy t
  rw [Scheme.Hom.ker_apply, RingHom.mem_ker] at h3
  rw [map_zero, show (homOfLE hsub) =
    (TopologicalSpace.Opens.map g.base).map (homOfLE (hDA t)) from Subsingleton.elim _ _]
  exact heq.trans h3

/-- The map on sections of the inclusion of an open subscheme, taken at that very open, is the
global-sections identification followed by a restriction. Both are isomorphisms; this records
which one. -/
theorem ι_app_self_eq (V : Y.Opens) :
    V.ι.app V = V.topIso.inv ≫ V.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ V))).op := by
  simp only [Scheme.Opens.ι_app, Scheme.Opens.toScheme_presheaf_map, Scheme.Opens.topIso_inv]
  exact (congrArg Y.presheaf.map (Subsingleton.elim _ _)).trans (Y.presheaf.map_comp _ _)

/-- Restriction from the whole open subscheme to the preimage of the open it sits over is an
isomorphism, that preimage being everything. -/
theorem isIso_restrict_ι_preimage_self (V : Y.Opens) :
    IsIso (V.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ V))).op) := by
  have hβ : (homOfLE (le_top (a := V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ V))) =
      eqToHom (Scheme.Opens.ι_preimage_self V) := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  rw [hβ, eqToHom_op]
  infer_instance

/-- The pushforward along the inclusion of an affine open `V` of the sheaf of ideals cut out by
an ideal `b` of `Γ(V, ⊤)` has, over `V` itself, exactly the ideal `b`. This is the one value of
the pushforward that has to be computed: its values over the basic opens of `V` then come from
the sheaf-of-ideals axiom. -/
theorem ideal_map_ofIdealTop_ι (V : Y.affineOpens) (b : Ideal Γ(V.1.toScheme, ⊤))
    (hqc : QuasiCompact V.1.ι) (H : IsAffineOpen (V.1.ι ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)) :
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop b).map V.1.ι).ideal V =
      Ideal.comap (V.1.topIso.inv).hom b := by
  have hiso := isIso_restrict_ι_preimage_self (Y := Y) V.1
  have hbij := ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    (V.1.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V.1.ι ⁻¹ᵁ V.1))).op)
  have hker : RingHom.ker
      (V.1.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V.1.ι ⁻¹ᵁ V.1))).op).hom = ⊥ :=
    (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mp hbij.1
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_map _ _ V H, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal,
    ι_app_self_eq V.1, CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← Ideal.comap_comap,
    Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective _ hbij.2, ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, hker, sup_bot_eq]

/-- On a quasi-separated scheme the intersection of two affine opens is covered by finitely
many basic opens of the first which are contained in the second. Quasi-separatedness makes the
intersection quasi-compact, and `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_basicOpen_le_affine_inter` produces
one such basic open through each of its points. -/
theorem exists_finset_basicOpen_cover_inter [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y] (V A : Y.affineOpens) :
    ∃ s : Finset Γ(Y, V.1), (∀ f : s, Y.basicOpen (f : Γ(Y, V.1)) ≤ A.1) ∧
      V.1 ⊓ A.1 ≤ ⨆ f : s, Y.basicOpen (f : Γ(Y, V.1)) := by
  classical
  have hcpt : IsCompact ((V.1 ⊓ A.1 : Y.Opens) : Set Y) := by
    rw [TopologicalSpace.Opens.coe_inf]
    exact QuasiSeparatedSpace.inter_isCompact _ _ V.1.2 V.2.isCompact A.1.2 A.2.isCompact
  have hpt : ∀ x ∈ (V.1 ⊓ A.1 : Y.Opens), ∃ f : Γ(Y, V.1),
      Y.basicOpen f ≤ A.1 ∧ x ∈ Y.basicOpen f := by
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨f, g, hfg, hxf⟩ := exists_basicOpen_le_affine_inter V.2 A.2 x hx
    exact ⟨f, hfg ▸ Y.basicOpen_le g, hxf⟩
  choose! f hfA hxf using hpt
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hcpt.elim_finite_subcover
    (fun x : (V.1 ⊓ A.1 : Y.Opens) ↦ ((Y.basicOpen (f x.1)) : Set Y))
    (fun x ↦ (Y.basicOpen (f x.1)).2) (fun x hx ↦ Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, hxf x hx⟩)
  refine ⟨t.image (fun x : (V.1 ⊓ A.1 : Y.Opens) ↦ f x.1), ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨x, -, hx⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 h.2
    exact hx ▸ hfA x.1 x.2
  · intro x hx
    obtain ⟨x', hx't, hxmem⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.1 (ht hx)
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨⟨f x'.1, Finset.mem_image.2 ⟨x', hx't, rfl⟩⟩, hxmem⟩

/-- **The two-chart step of Properties, Tag 01PF read at a sheaf of ideals.** Given a sheaf of
ideals `J` finitely generated over each member of a finite family of affine opens, and one more
affine open `V`, there is a sheaf of ideals below `J` which agrees with `J` over every member of
the family, is finitely generated over `V` as well, and still contains a prescribed finite set
of sections over `V`.

The new sheaf of ideals is `J ⊓ E`, where `E` is the pushforward along `V.ι` of the sheaf of
ideals on `V` cut out by a finitely generated `b ≤ J.ideal V` chosen — by
`Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_fg_le_forall_map_eq` — to agree with `J` over finitely many
basic opens of `V` covering the intersections of `V` with the family. Over `V` the intersection
is `b`, and over each member `A` of the family `J.ideal A ≤ E.ideal A` by
`Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.mem_ker_ideal_of_forall_restrict`, applied to those basic opens:
they cover the preimage of `A` under the morphism cutting out `E`, because that morphism factors
through `V`. -/
theorem exists_le_fg_at_chart [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y] (J : Y.IdealSheafData)
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (W : ι → Y.affineOpens) (hWfg : ∀ k, (J.ideal (W k)).FG)
    (V : Y.affineOpens) (s : Finset Γ(Y, V.1)) (hs : ∀ y ∈ s, y ∈ J.ideal V) :
    ∃ J' : Y.IdealSheafData, J' ≤ J ∧ (∀ k, J'.ideal (W k) = J.ideal (W k)) ∧
      (J'.ideal V).FG ∧ (∀ y ∈ s, y ∈ J'.ideal V) := by
  classical
  choose t htA htcov using fun k ↦ exists_finset_basicOpen_cover_inter V (W k)
  have hFG : ∀ d : (k : ι) × {f : Γ(Y, V.1) // f ∈ t k},
      ((J.ideal V).map
        (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1)))).op).hom).FG := by
    intro d
    rw [J.map_ideal_basicOpen V (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1))]
    exact fg_ideal_of_le (htA d.1 ⟨d.2.1, d.2.2⟩) (hWfg d.1)
  obtain ⟨b₁, hb₁le, hb₁fg, hb₁eq⟩ := exists_fg_le_forall_map_eq
    (fun d : (k : ι) × {f : Γ(Y, V.1) // f ∈ t k} ↦
      (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1)))).op).hom) (J.ideal V) hFG
  set b : Ideal Γ(Y, V.1) := b₁ ⊔ Ideal.span (s : Set Γ(Y, V.1)) with hbdef
  have hble : b ≤ J.ideal V := sup_le hb₁le (Ideal.span_le.2 (fun y hy ↦ hs y hy))
  have hbfg : b.FG := Submodule.FG.sup hb₁fg (Submodule.fg_span (Set.toFinite _))
  have hbeq : ∀ d : (k : ι) × {f : Γ(Y, V.1) // f ∈ t k},
      b.map (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1)))).op).hom =
        (J.ideal V).map (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1)))).op).hom :=
    fun d ↦ le_antisymm (Ideal.map_mono hble) (hb₁eq d ▸ Ideal.map_mono le_sup_left)
  have hqc : QuasiCompact V.1.ι := by
    have : CompactSpace V.1.toScheme := by have := V.2; infer_instance
    infer_instance
  have H : IsAffineOpen (V.1.ι ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) := by
    have := V.2
    rw [Scheme.Opens.ι_preimage_self]
    exact isAffineOpen_top _
  set c : V.1.toScheme.IdealSheafData :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.comap (V.1.topIso.hom).hom b) with hc
  set E : Y.IdealSheafData := c.map V.1.ι with hE
  have heV : E.ideal V = b := by
    rw [hE, hc, ideal_map_ofIdealTop_ι V _ hqc H, Ideal.comap_comap,
      show (V.1.topIso.hom).hom.comp (V.1.topIso.inv).hom = RingHom.id _ by
        rw [← CommRingCat.hom_comp, V.1.topIso.inv_hom_id]; rfl,
      Ideal.comap_id]
  have heD : ∀ d : (k : ι) × {f : Γ(Y, V.1) // f ∈ t k},
      E.ideal (Y.affineBasicOpen (U := V) (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1)))
        = J.ideal (Y.affineBasicOpen (U := V) (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1))) := by
    intro d
    rw [← E.map_ideal_basicOpen V (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1)), heV, hbeq d,
      J.map_ideal_basicOpen V (d.2 : Γ(Y, V.1))]
  have hgker : E = (c.subschemeι ≫ V.1.ι).ker := rfl
  have hkey : ∀ k, J.ideal (W k) ≤ E.ideal (W k) := by
    intro k y hy
    rw [hgker]
    refine mem_ker_ideal_of_forall_restrict _ (W k)
      (fun f : (t k) ↦ Y.affineBasicOpen (U := V) (f : Γ(Y, V.1)))
      (fun f ↦ htA k f) ?_ ?_
    · intro z hz
      have hzW : (V.1.ι.base) (c.subschemeι.base z) ∈ (W k).1 := hz
      have hzV : (V.1.ι.base) (c.subschemeι.base z) ∈ V.1 :=
        (Scheme.Opens.range_ι V.1).le (Set.mem_range_self _)
      obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.1 (htcov k ⟨hzV, hzW⟩)
      exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨f, hf⟩
    · intro f
      rw [← hgker, heD ⟨k, f⟩, ← J.map_ideal (htA k f)]
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hy
  refine ⟨J ⊓ E, inf_le_left, fun k ↦ ?_, ?_, fun y hy ↦ ?_⟩
  · change J.ideal (W k) ⊓ E.ideal (W k) = J.ideal (W k)
    exact inf_eq_left.2 (hkey k)
  · have hJV : (J ⊓ E).ideal V = b := by
      change J.ideal V ⊓ E.ideal V = b
      rw [heV]
      exact inf_eq_right.2 hble
    rw [hJV]
    exact hbfg
  · have hmem : y ∈ b := by
      rw [hbdef]
      exact Submodule.mem_sup_right (Ideal.subset_span hy)
    change y ∈ J.ideal V ⊓ E.ideal V
    exact ⟨hs y hy, heV ▸ hmem⟩

/-- **The induction of Properties, Tag 01PF read at a sheaf of ideals.** Absorbing the affine
opens of a list one at a time by
`Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_le_fg_at_chart`, a sheaf of ideals which is finitely
generated over one affine open `V₀` and contains a prescribed finite set of sections there is
cut down to one which is moreover finitely generated over every affine open of the list.

The list is absorbed from the back: the induction hypothesis is applied first, and the extra
chart is absorbed last, against the family consisting of `V₀` together with the entries of the
tail. That order is what lets the step see all the opens whose values it must not disturb. -/
theorem exists_le_fg_of_list [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y] (K : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (V₀ : Y.affineOpens) (s : Finset Γ(Y, V₀.1)) :
    ∀ (L : List Y.affineOpens) (J : Y.IdealSheafData), J ≤ K →
      (∀ y ∈ s, y ∈ J.ideal V₀) → (J.ideal V₀).FG →
      ∃ J' : Y.IdealSheafData, J' ≤ K ∧ (∀ y ∈ s, y ∈ J'.ideal V₀) ∧
        (J'.ideal V₀).FG ∧ ∀ A ∈ L, (J'.ideal A).FG := by
  intro L
  induction L with
  | nil => exact fun J hJK hs hfg ↦ ⟨J, hJK, hs, hfg, by simp⟩
  | cons V L' ih =>
    intro J hJK hs hfg
    obtain ⟨J₁, hJ₁K, hJ₁s, hJ₁fg, hJ₁L⟩ := ih J hJK hs hfg
    obtain ⟨J₂, hJ₂le, hJ₂eq, hJ₂fg, -⟩ := exists_le_fg_at_chart J₁
      (ι := Option (Fin L'.length))
      (fun o ↦ match o with | none => V₀ | some i => L'[(i : ℕ)])
      (fun o ↦ by
        match o with
        | none => exact hJ₁fg
        | some i => exact hJ₁L _ (List.getElem_mem _))
      V (∅ : Finset Γ(Y, V.1)) (by simp)
    have hV₀ : J₂.ideal V₀ = J₁.ideal V₀ := hJ₂eq none
    refine ⟨J₂, hJ₂le.trans hJ₁K, fun y hy ↦ ?_, ?_, fun A hA ↦ ?_⟩
    · rw [hV₀]
      exact hJ₁s y hy
    · rw [hV₀]
      exact hJ₁fg
    · rcases List.mem_cons.1 hA with rfl | hA'
      · exact hJ₂fg
      · obtain ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩ := List.mem_iff_getElem.1 hA'
        rw [hJ₂eq (some ⟨i, hi⟩)]
        exact hJ₁L _ (List.getElem_mem _)

/-- A sheaf of ideals on a locally Noetherian scheme is finitely generated over every affine
open, because the sections there form a Noetherian ring. -/
theorem fg_ideal_of_isLocallyNoetherian [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (A : Y.affineOpens) : (I.ideal A).FG := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(Y, A.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian A
  exact IsNoetherian.noetherian _

end Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Over a locally Noetherian scheme every closed subscheme is of finite presentation: a closed
immersion is always of finite type, and Morphisms, Tag 01TX turns finite type into finite
presentation over a locally Noetherian base. -/
@[ega "IV 20.3.8.7" "special case",
  sga "1 IX 4.10" "closed immersions",
  sga "1 IX 4.7" "special case",
  sga "3 V 6.1" "special case"]
theorem finitePresentation_subschemeι_of_isLocallyNoetherian [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    (I : Y.IdealSheafData) : FinitePresentation I.subschemeι :=
  finitePresentation_of_finiteType I.subschemeι

/-- **Properties, Tag 01PG at a sheaf of ideals, for a locally Noetherian scheme.** A
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on a locally Noetherian scheme is the supremum of the sheaves of
ideals below it cutting out finite-presentation closed subschemes — trivially so, since it is
itself one of them. -/
theorem isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_isLocallyNoetherian [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    (K : Y.IdealSheafData) : K.IsSupOfFinitePresentation :=
  le_antisymm (iSup_le_of_finitePresentationSubscheme K)
    (le_iSup_of_le ⟨K, finitePresentation_subschemeι_of_isLocallyNoetherian K, le_refl K⟩ le_rfl)

/-- Limits, Tag 09ZP for a locally Noetherian target: a closed subscheme of a locally
Noetherian scheme is the limit, in `Over Y`, of the finite-presentation closed subschemes of
`Y` containing it. The tag itself is stated for a quasi-compact and quasi-separated target, so
`@[stacks 09ZP]` is withheld here and placed on
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLimit_finitePresentationCone_of_qcqs` instead. -/
def isLimit_finitePresentationCone_of_isLocallyNoetherian {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion f] :
    IsLimit (finitePresentationCone f (le_refl f.ker)) :=
  isLimit_finitePresentationCone_ker f (isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_isLocallyNoetherian f.ker)

/-- **Properties, Tag 01PG at a sheaf of ideals.** On a quasi-compact and quasi-separated
scheme a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals is the supremum of the sheaves of ideals below it which
cut out closed subschemes of finite presentation.

The reduction to single sections is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_forall_mem`, which is the source's own proof of
Tag 01PG; what remains is Tag 01PF read at a sheaf of ideals, supplied here by
`Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_le_fg_of_list` over a finite affine cover and then spread to
every affine open by `Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.fg_ideal_of_fg_cover`. The first chart
absorbed is the affine open carrying the section, with the empty family of opens to preserve. -/
theorem isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_qcqs [CompactSpace Y] [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y]
    (K : Y.IdealSheafData) : K.IsSupOfFinitePresentation := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := (IsOpenCover.mk (iSup_affineOpens_eq_top Y)).exists_finite_of_compactSpace
  refine isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_forall_mem K (fun U x hx ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨J₀, hJ₀K, -, hJ₀fg, hJ₀s⟩ := Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_le_fg_at_chart K
    (ι := Empty) (fun e ↦ e.elim) (fun e ↦ e.elim) U {x}
    (by
      intro y hy
      rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hy
      exact hy ▸ hx)
  obtain ⟨J, hJK, hJs, -, hJL⟩ := Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.exists_le_fg_of_list K U {x}
    σ.toList J₀ hJ₀K hJ₀s hJ₀fg
  refine ⟨J, ?_, hJK, hJs x (Finset.mem_singleton_self x)⟩
  rw [finitePresentation_subschemeι_iff]
  exact Stacks.IdealSheafFiniteType.fg_ideal_of_fg_cover J
    (fun i : σ ↦ (i.1 : Y.affineOpens)) hσ.iSup_eq_top
    (fun i ↦ hJL _ (Finset.mem_toList.2 i.2))

/-- **Limits, Tag 09ZP.** The source of a closed immersion into a quasi-compact and
quasi-separated scheme `Y` is the limit, in `Over Y`, of the inverse system of
finite-presentation closed subschemes of `Y` containing it.

The index of that system is `Stacks.Flatness.FinitePresentationSubscheme f.ker`, whose every
member is by definition a closed subscheme of `Y` of finite presentation, so the tag's
assertion about the stages is carried by the statement itself; the directedness of the system
is the unconditional
`AlgebraicGeometry.isCofiltered_finitePresentationSubscheme_op`, which is the other half of the
covering set and is left untagged where it stands. -/
@[stacks 09ZP]
def isLimit_finitePresentationCone_of_qcqs {X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace Y]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion f] :
    IsLimit (finitePresentationCone f (le_refl f.ker)) :=
  isLimit_finitePresentationCone_ker f (isSupOfFinitePresentation_of_qcqs f.ker)

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
